  "description": "Pachkili is a parrot-faced play tower in yellow and green that works as a small circuit. Children climb a curved net climber, crawl through a tube tunnel and slide back down, then run round to start again. The name and the face come from the parrot, and the loop keeps children moving from one activity to the next. Up to 15 children aged 5 to 12 can play on it. At 13'4\" x 4'5\", with a safe play area of 18'4\" x 8'5\", it is narrow enough for a side lawn or a school corridor of open ground. Climbing and crawling build upper body strength and spatial awareness. We cover the main materials for 3 years. Measure the strip you have in mind and we will tell you if it fits.",
